WEBVTT

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
BISMI ALLAH AL-RAHMAN AL-RAHIM. In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Brothers and sisters AL-Salãmu ‘Alaykum. The Friday congregational prayer is an

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.000
obligatory duty upon every Muslim man and woman. This is a social function

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.000
decreed by God Almighty for the Muslims to get together and to know each other

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.000
and to be familiar with their problems and their joys. And we find in SURA

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:14.000
number 62 verse number 9, the commandment from God says o you who believe when the

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.000
contact prayers, the SALAT for Friday, is announced, you shall go to the mosque and

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
observe the SALAT prayer, and drop all business. This is better for

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
you if you only knew. So, if anyone is afraid that he or she may lose some

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
business during the Friday prayer, God is saying this should be better for you

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.000
God will make it up to you. God runs the world and He is the only

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.000
provider and He guarantees you doing better if you go to the Friday prayer.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
And notice that the commandment said o you who believe.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.000
It didn't say o you believing men or o you believing women. It says o you who

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.000
believe when the contact prayer on Friday is called for, you shall go and

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.000
drop all business. It is very important. I'm emphasizing the role of the women

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.000
because this is also an educational meeting where people sit down and

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
listen to a sermon and the Muslim woman must be the best educated because she

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.000
teaches the children. Women are our mothers and they teach

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:26.000
us as we grow up and it is essential that they are educated, not ignorant.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:33.000
The traditional customary Muslims of the Middle East, they kept the women away

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.000
from the mosque and this kept the children ignorant because the mothers

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
are ignorant as far as the religion is concerned. So, it is very important to

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.000
emphasize this fact that Muslim men and women are required. It is an obligatory

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
duty for them to go to the Friday prayer.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Now, there are certain conditions for the Friday prayer. The people dress nicely as

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:29.000
commanded in the Quran, and they go for the noon prayer on Friday to the mosque.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:35.000
And the Imam or the person who gives the sermon is required to follow certain

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.000
traditions. These are religious traditions or duties that came to us all

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.000
the way from Abraham and it is universal. This is the way it is happening all over the world.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.000
The first condition is that throughout

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.000
the prayer from the beginning to the end, you mention only the name of God, ALLAH

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.000
SUBHANAHU WA TA'ALA in the AZAN. The AZAN should be ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.000
ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR, La Elaha Ella Allah. This is the AZAN.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Now, the AZAN should be ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:34.000
ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR, La Elaha Ella Allah. This is the AZAN. So, the AZAN or the call for

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.000
contact prayer is delivered. Then, the Imam stands up in front of the

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:46.000
congregation and he starts the first sermon by saying ALHAMDU LILLAH.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:52.000
This is the first requirement. Now, you notice I said the first sermon,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:58.000
because the KHUTBA or sermon on Friday consists of two sections or two sermons.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:06.000
The prayer itself consists of two RAKATs, instead of four. The customary noon prayer

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.000
consists of four RAKATs or four units but on Friday, it is only two

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:17.000
RAKATs or two units and this is because the two sermons compensate for two

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:23.000
RAKATs or two units. So, the first sermon and also the second sermon, they must

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:32.000
begin by stating ALHAMDU LILLAH, praise be to God, followed by the SHAHADA.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:40.000
And the SHAHADA, as dictated in the Quran, in SURA number 3 verse 81, the SHAHADA is

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:46.000
La Elaha Ella Allah. That's it. So, the Imam stands up and he begins

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:53.000
each sermon the first one and the second one by saying ALHAMDU LILLAH. La Elaha Ella Allah.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Then, he goes into the sermon, the subject in any language that he wishes.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Of course, in this country in the united states, it'll be English,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:12.000
so the people will understand. If the Imam, during the sermon, uses Quran in Arabic,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.000
he must translate it, so the people will understand. This is the whole idea of a sermon.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:24.000
The sermon also deals with the local conditions of the local community.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Or it can deal with a general lesson from the Quran or a general religious lesson.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
So, let me write for you the first requirement

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:40.000
which is stating ALHAMDU LILLAH. La Elaha Ella Allah. at the beginning of each sermon.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
The Imam stands up for the sermon and the first thing he

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:24.000
says in the first sermon and the second sermon is ALHAMDU LILLAH. This is how it looks in writing.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:44.000
AL-Hamdu Lillah,

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.000
which means praise be to God.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:56.000
La Elaha Ella Allah, which looks like this. La means no.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:010:01.000
Elaha means god with a small g.

00:010:01.000 --> 00:010:08.000
La Elaha Ella, except

00:010:08.000 --> 00:010:17.000
Ella Allah.

00:010:17.000 --> 00:010:24.000
La Elaha Ella Allah. There is no god except Allah.

00:010:24.000 --> 00:010:28.000
This is the required utterance at the beginning of the first sermon and the

00:010:28.000 --> 00:010:34.000
second sermon. After this, you go into the subject of your sermon. Now, you notice

00:010:34.000 --> 00:010:41.000
I didn't say anything else. This is what you start with. ALHAMDU LILLAH. La Elaha Ella Allah.

00:010:41.000 --> 00:010:44.000
You don't start with BISMI ALLAH AL-RAHMAN AL-RAHIM, or dear

00:010:44.000 --> 00:010:48.000
brothers and sisters or AL-Salãmu ‘Alaykum or anything else.

00:010:48.000 --> 00:010:54.000
The minute you stand up for the sermon, you say ALHAMDU LILLAH. La Elaha Ella Allah.

00:010:54.000 --> 00:010:58.000
Then, you can say dear brothers and sisters, AL-Salãmu ‘Alaykum. I want to talk

00:010:58.000 --> 00:011:04.000
to you today about the contact prayers, the SALAT, for example, or whatever your subject is.

00:011:23.000 --> 00:011:30.000
After you finish the subject of the first sermon, how do you finish the first sermon?

00:011:30.000 --> 00:011:34.000
You finish it by asking the people to repent. You can ask them in

00:011:34.000 --> 00:011:42.000
Arabic and then translate it to English. And the Arabic is Tooboo Ela Allah. Repent.

00:011:42.000 --> 00:011:48.000
This is how you end the first sermon. Let me write it for you.

00:011:48.000 --> 00:011:54.000
Tooboo means repent, plural.

00:011:54.000 --> 00:012:03.000
Ela Allah.

00:012:03.000 --> 00:012:11.000
Tooboo Ela Allah. And this is how you end the first sermon.

00:012:11.000 --> 00:012:16.000
Now, as soon as you say Tooboo Ela Allah. Repent,

00:012:16.000 --> 00:012:21.000
you sit down and you repent yourself. You sit down and you pray to

00:012:21.000 --> 00:012:25.000
God please, God forgive me. I repent to you. I will never commit a sin after

00:012:25.000 --> 00:012:27.000
after now, and you mean it.

00:012:27.000 --> 00:012:32.000
Now, as soon as you say Tooboo Ela Allah to end the first sermon,

00:012:32.000 --> 00:012:37.000
you sit down yourself and you repent. You ask God to forgive you.

00:012:37.000 --> 00:012:40.000
So, here's how you end the first sermon.

00:012:40.000 --> 00:012:46.000
You finish your subject, then you say to the people Tooboo Ela Allah. Repent.

00:012:46.000 --> 00:012:48.000
And then you sit down

00:012:48.000 --> 00:012:55.000
and you ask God to forgive you and you declare your repentance.

00:012:55.000 --> 00:013:00.000
You say please, God forgive me. I repent. I will never commit a sin after now. And you

00:013:00.000 --> 00:013:05.000
mean it. Of course, you're gonna fall in sin again, but God says He loves those

00:013:05.000 --> 00:013:13.000
who continuously repent. So, you sit down for about a minute, no more, just one minute.

00:013:13.000 --> 00:013:16.000
And everybody in the mosque will be asking God for forgiveness.

00:013:16.000 --> 00:013:21.000
And everyone at the mosque will be repenting, and then you stand up for the

00:013:21.000 --> 00:013:27.000
second sermon. And you start the second sermon by - that's right - ALHAMDU LILLAH.

00:013:27.000 --> 00:013:31.000
La Elaha Ella Allah. This is how you start the second sermon

00:013:31.000 --> 00:013:37.000
exactly the same way as the first sermon. Then, you either continue the subject you were

00:013:37.000 --> 00:013:42.000
talking about in the first sermon, or you talk about a new subject. You can have

00:013:42.000 --> 00:013:48.000
two different subjects for the two sermons. And after you finish talking in

00:013:48.000 --> 00:013:53.000
the second sermon, you end this last sermon by saying

00:013:53.000 --> 00:013:59.000
Aqem Al-Salah. And this is a sign to someone in the congregation to declare

00:013:59.000 --> 00:014:05.000
that the SALAT, the contact prayer for Friday, is ready to be observed and

00:014:05.000 --> 00:014:07.000
everybody stands up.

00:014:07.000 --> 00:014:11.000
You end the sermon by saying Aqem Al-Salah. Let me write it for you.

00:014:16.000 --> 00:014:20.000
Aqem

00:014:20.000 --> 00:014:26.000
Al-Salah

00:014:27.000 --> 00:014:31.000
Aqem Al-Salah

00:014:31.000 --> 00:014:36.000
Now, the minute you say Aqem Al-Salah, the second sermon is over,

00:014:36.000 --> 00:014:41.000
and a person in the congregation will say ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR

00:014:41.000 --> 00:014:48.000
ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR, La Elaha Ella Allah. And this means everybody stand

00:014:48.000 --> 00:014:53.000
up and let us pray. Then, as the Imam who gave the two

00:014:53.000 --> 00:014:59.000
sermons, you stand up in front of the congregation and you pray two RAKATs as usual.

00:014:59.000 --> 00:015:07.000
And I'm going to show you now an example of Friday congregation sermons.

00:015:07.000 --> 00:015:10.000
God bless you.

00:015:36.000 --> 00:015:41.000
So, let me summarize for you. You begin the first sermon by saying ALHAMDU LILLAH.

00:015:41.000 --> 00:015:47.000
La Elaha Ella Allah. Then, you go into your subject in English. Then, you end the

00:015:47.000 --> 00:015:52.000
first sermon by saying Tooboo Ela Allah. Then, you sit down and you ask God for

00:015:52.000 --> 00:015:57.000
forgiveness and you repent. You sit down for about one minute, no more than that.

00:015:57.000 --> 00:016:02.000
Then, you stand up and you start the second sermon by saying the same thing

00:016:02.000 --> 00:016:07.000
ALHAMDU LILLAH. La Elaha Ella Allah. Then, you go into your subject that you want

00:016:07.000 --> 00:016:13.000
to talk about and you end the second sermon by saying Aqem Al-Salah.

00:016:13.000 --> 00:016:18.000
When you say that, someone in the congregation that knows that he was

00:016:18.000 --> 00:016:22.000
going to do this, will stand up and say ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR,

00:016:22.000 --> 00:016:29.000
ALLAH-O AKBAR, ALLAH-O AKBAR, La Elaha Ella Allah. And then, everyone in the mosque stands up and

00:016:29.000 --> 00:016:35.000
they line... they stand up in straight lines behind you, the Imam. You take your

00:016:35.000 --> 00:016:41.000
place and you do the Friday prayer exactly like the morning prayer. It is

00:016:41.000 --> 00:016:47.000
identical to the morning prayer because it consists of only two RAKATs, or two units.

00:016:47.000 --> 00:016:52.000
Now, the exact method of doing the SALAT, the contact prayers, is explained

00:016:52.000 --> 00:016:56.000
in our tape entitled principles of Muslim prayer.

00:016:56.000 --> 00:017:02.000
This gives the details of all five daily contact prayers.

00:017:26.000 --> 00:017:32.000
ALHAMDU LILLAH, WA ASHHADU AN LA ILAHA ILLA ALLAH, WAHDAHU LA SHARIKA LAH.

00:017:32.000 --> 00:017:38.000
Praise be to God and we bear witness that there's only one God.

00:017:38.000 --> 00:017:43.000
I want to start my KHUTBA this time with the beautiful quotation

00:017:43.000 --> 00:017:52.000
from the Bible from Luke 12:29 to 31. It is, of course, a Quranic idea. The

00:017:52.000 --> 00:018:00.000
author is one and the same. And this is expressed beautifully in English.

00:018:00.000 --> 00:018:03.000
Starting at 29, it says it is not for you

00:018:03.000 --> 00:018:11.000
to be in search of what you are to eat or drink. Stop worrying.

00:018:11.000 --> 00:018:16.000
The unbelievers of this world are always running after these things.

00:018:16.000 --> 00:018:24.000
God knows that you need such things. Seek out, instead, His kingship over you

00:018:24.000 --> 00:018:28.000
and the rest will follow in turn. So, all you need to do is seek

00:018:28.000 --> 00:018:35.000
God's kingship over you and everything else you need follows, the food, the

00:018:35.000 --> 00:018:40.000
provisions, the clothing, the health, everything else follows.

00:018:40.000 --> 00:018:46.000
So, what does this mean? What does seeking God's Kingship mean?

00:018:46.000 --> 00:018:52.000
It means that you give priority to God's commandments. You give priority to the

00:018:52.000 --> 00:018:57.000
five contact prayers. You wake up in the morning and you say my duty today is to

00:018:57.000 --> 00:019:01.000
do the five contact prayers.

00:019:03.000 --> 00:019:07.000
That you... the Friday prayer is a commandment from God. There is a

00:019:07.000 --> 00:019:13.000
commandment in Sura 60, verse 9, that you must go to the Friday prayer. You give this priority.

00:019:13.000 --> 00:019:18.000
You arrange your life and your job and your circumstances,

00:019:18.000 --> 00:019:24.000
so you will do the five daily prayers and the Friday prayer.

00:019:24.000 --> 00:019:27.000
And of course, you people here are the least people who need this. Some people

00:019:27.000 --> 00:019:33.000
out there are the ones who need this kind of reminder.

00:019:33.000 --> 00:019:38.000
You put on the list of your priorities the Quranic study. There's a Quranic

00:019:38.000 --> 00:019:44.000
study every Friday night going on here, where we study the Word of God.

00:019:44.000 --> 00:019:49.000
And you have to work your circumstances. You cannot be somewhere in Tucson and there's

00:019:49.000 --> 00:019:53.000
a Quranic study going on in the mosque.

00:019:53.000 --> 00:019:59.000
Otherwise, you don't really care. You're not seeking God's Kinship over you. To be

00:019:59.000 --> 00:020:07.000
sitting within say 50 miles and there's a Quranic study going on.

00:020:07.000 --> 00:020:11.000
What does it mean to seek God's kinship over you and everything else follows, the

00:020:11.000 --> 00:020:18.000
provisions, the health, the happiness? You give priority to the activities

00:020:18.000 --> 00:020:24.000
of the believers. You remember the verse in SURA 18 that says force yourself

00:020:24.000 --> 00:020:29.000
to be with those who worship God alone, because it takes some effort and some

00:020:29.000 --> 00:020:34.000
work. It's not easy but this is what is good for you, as you'll see in the

00:020:34.000 --> 00:020:38.000
second KHUTBA, IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:020:38.000 --> 00:020:42.000
It means that you make a point of giving out the ZAKAT. charity, as

00:020:42.000 --> 00:020:47.000
commanded by God. This is how you seek God's Kingship over you.

00:020:47.000 --> 00:020:53.000
One day in the year, whatever January 1st, December 31st, the first day of Ramadan,

00:020:53.000 --> 00:020:59.000
any day you set for yourself, one day in the year. You calculate exactly how

00:020:59.000 --> 00:021:04.000
much you are worth and you give out two and a half percent to people that you

00:021:04.000 --> 00:021:11.000
know, personally, people who need your charity. And the Quran gives the exact

00:021:11.000 --> 00:021:16.000
order, your parents first. If they don't need it, then your relatives, your cousins

00:021:16.000 --> 00:021:23.000
your brothers, sisters. I mean, your genetic brothers and sisters. And if all

00:021:23.000 --> 00:021:27.000
your relatives are rich, they don't need it, then you go to the orphans, children

00:021:27.000 --> 00:021:34.000
who have no support, one of the parents is missing somehow.

00:021:34.000 --> 00:021:40.000
And after that the traveling stranger, somebody stranded from Mexico or

00:021:40.000 --> 00:021:45.000
Nicaragua or whatever and passes by your house or you know personally, people who

00:021:45.000 --> 00:021:49.000
immigrated from Thailand or Vietnam and they're living in a house in a terrible

00:021:49.000 --> 00:021:54.000
conditions and you know them. Then, they come next. So, there is a specific

00:021:54.000 --> 00:022:00.000
sequence or order to give out this charity.

00:022:01.000 --> 00:022:06.000
You give priority to HAJJ, eventually, not now. I wouldn't advise you to

00:022:06.000 --> 00:022:12.000
do it now. The Quran makes it conditional. Someday all of us, IN SHAA ALLAH, we'll go.

00:022:12.000 --> 00:022:17.000
We're gonna charter a plane when we'll go all of us. We'll make HAJJ and we'll go

00:022:17.000 --> 00:022:20.000
in as there will be great victory, because the land over there will be

00:022:20.000 --> 00:022:24.000
worshiping God alone. This is God's promise to us and

00:022:24.000 --> 00:022:31.000
therefore I can talk about it in this way. So eventually, you have to observe HAJJ.

00:022:31.000 --> 00:022:38.000
You seek God's Kingship over you and everything else follows by observing the

00:022:38.000 --> 00:022:44.000
prohibitions that God gave you. You don't drink. You don't gamble.

00:022:44.000 --> 00:022:51.000
You don't eat pork. You don't lie. You don't cheat. You don't

00:022:51.000 --> 00:022:56.000
violate your promises. You must be a person of your word.

00:022:56.000 --> 00:023:03.000
You must be an example of a person of God, one a member in God's Kingdom.

00:023:08.000 --> 00:023:16.000
Anything else in your life must take place number two. You give priority to

00:023:16.000 --> 00:023:20.000
these activities, the commands of God, and this way you seek God's Kingship over you

00:023:20.000 --> 00:023:27.000
and this way, you attain all other goals: money, health, wealth,

00:023:27.000 --> 00:023:32.000
happiness et cetera, et cetera. Tooboo Ela Allah. Repent.

00:023:43.000 --> 00:023:51.000
ALHAMDU LILLAH, WA ASHHADU AN LA ILAHA ILLA ALLAH, WAHDAHU LA SHARIKA LAH.

00:023:51.000 --> 00:023:58.000
By studying the Quran continuously, we have discovered the secret of happiness.

00:023:58.000 --> 00:024:02.000
The secret of happiness is a developed, nourished and growing soul, the real you,

00:024:02.000 --> 00:024:08.000
the real person, not this body. This is the secret of happiness and we

00:024:08.000 --> 00:024:13.000
came to this conclusion by studying people who obtained everything. They got

00:024:13.000 --> 00:024:22.000
everything that the human beings go after: money, fame, good looks, sports cars,

00:024:22.000 --> 00:024:28.000
whatever. And I have used the example of Eddie Murphy, a movie star, when he was

00:024:28.000 --> 00:024:35.000
interviewed by Barbara Walters. He's got millions of dollars. He got palaces in

00:024:35.000 --> 00:024:42.000
California exclusive places and in New Jersey, five luxurious cars, all the

00:024:42.000 --> 00:024:48.000
girls, all the money, all the fame that he wants, and he told Barbara Walters he was

00:024:48.000 --> 00:024:52.000
not happy. So, what is the secret of... Aren't these the things that people are

00:024:52.000 --> 00:025:00.000
going after, money and fame and wealth and whatever? And he's not happy. So, the

00:025:00.000 --> 00:025:05.000
secret of happiness is that he must develop his soul and the soul can be

00:025:05.000 --> 00:025:10.000
developed by worshiping God alone.

00:025:10.000 --> 00:025:13.000
Now this KHUTBA,

00:025:13.000 --> 00:025:19.000
I want to talk about God's name: AL-RAZAQ, the provider, the provider. God is

00:025:19.000 --> 00:025:26.000
the exclusive provider. He's the one who decides how much money

00:025:26.000 --> 00:025:31.000
you're going to make or you made from birth to death.

00:025:31.000 --> 00:025:37.000
And I want to shed a whole new light on this word: the provider, because God

00:025:37.000 --> 00:025:41.000
provides for the body and for the soul.

00:025:41.000 --> 00:025:50.000
Therefore, the contact prayers that you do five times a day are a provision from God.

00:025:50.000 --> 00:025:53.000
The duties that I talked about in the first KHUTBA,

00:025:53.000 --> 00:025:59.000
they're actually a gift from God. And we see this... there's a lot of

00:025:59.000 --> 00:026:03.000
evidence in the Quran for this.

00:026:03.000 --> 00:026:09.000
For example, in SURA 7 verse 43, we see that the people in Heaven pray and say

00:026:09.000 --> 00:026:14.000
